  "headline": "Government Reaffirms Ujung Kulon Status Amid Rhino Relocation Talk",
  "seoTitle": "Government Reaffirms Ujung Kulon Status",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian officials emphasize Ujung Kulon remains the primary habitat for Javan rhinos, addressing concerns over potential mining and relocation plans.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Government officials confirmed Ujung Kulon National Park remains the core habitat for Javan rhinos.",
    "Proposals for a second habitat in Alas Purwo and Baluran are undergoing ongoing assessment.",
    "Authorities are moving to remove waters surrounding the park from designated mining zones."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government has clarified its stance on the preservation of Ujung Kulon National Park following public discourse regarding the potential relocation of Javan rhinos. Minister of Forestry Raja Juli stated that the park remains the primary habitat for the species, while plans for alternative locations like Alas Purwo and Baluran are being evaluated. Concurrently, the Minister of Environment has requested that the maritime areas around Ujung Kulon be removed from authorized mining zones to ensure ecological safety. These developments follow concerns from various stakeholders, including political figures and non-governmental organizations like WWF-Indonesia, who have called for rigorous scientific study regarding any potential population shifts. The government continues to prioritize protection measures, noting that recent conservation efforts have yielded new births within the existing Ujung Kulon ecosystem.",
